{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793312554,"nonce":"HnyNEYcT4mf5nT7VM7FG+nm3YKk=","message":"Fixed in 909f1977, Keep JIT promotion budgets out of AOT compilation.\n\nAOT now drains pending compilation without the shared JIT budget. JIT policy is preserved. This removes the repeated whole-module scans and all 2,747 compiler-created table trampolines from Pocket Studio; 2,699 bytecode bodies still compile, and LLVM definitions fall from 7,160 to 4,413.\n\nThe original demo bytecode is identical in the primary before/after comparison (2,138,419 bytes, SHA-256 3f7903172336a0e49ceae291c4104982dec9f7050ac60bbd26ebde4014322e72). It was rebuilt from the current demo with published Ashui/components/icons 0.2.2, full Haxe DCE, the WASM define and RayDE preview I/O adapter. The old 0.1.5 bin/web artifact was not used. No source/workload reduction or optimization-level change was made.\n\nNUC, matched LLVM 21.1.8 host release O3/ThinLTO/16-CU compilers, RayDE preview settings (AIR/LLVM O3, codegen 0, fibers, six shards). Three measured reversed-order runs per compiler after warm-ups, with no concurrent NUC Rust builds. Every measured run hits all 2,699 optimized AIR bodies.\n\nMedian wall: 20.525 -\u003e 6.984 s, -66.0%, 2.9x faster.\nLLVM IR stage: 14.125 -\u003e 0.933 s.\nLLVM backend: 5.067 -\u003e 4.922 s.\nLink: 0.933 -\u003e 0.899 s.\nProcess CPU: 41.235 -\u003e 26.813 s.\nWASM: 18,621,509 -\u003e 18,580,879 bytes.\n\nSeparate fixed compiler samples: disabled 7.283 s, cold 7.685 s, warm 7.187 s, one-function edit 7.235 s (2,697 optimized hits, three entries written). The edit changes one byte of bytecode. Fixed original output matches the cap-off diagnostic byte-for-byte.\n\nValidation: new native/WASM cap-independence regression passes on NUC and Mac, varying caps 1/256/off and exercising virtual-method closures, a getter and catches (expected 50; identical WASM artifacts across caps). All 13 native AOT smoke programs match JIT output. Original/fixed/edited NUC modules render the actual eight-task board in Chrome with the preview filesystem channel; screenshots are byte-identical, SHA-256 32162fded7eaa567ac4741f2b579e07822c3c7baad7363806b185b25642e6bfb. Clippy passes. Mac release binary rebuilt and tested.\n\nReport, exact configuration, individual samples and phase profiles: docs/wasm/rayde-demo-build-times.md and rayde-demo-build-time-results.json.\n\nThe corrected remaining cost is predominantly backend (~4.9 s, including O3 middle-end and eager whole-stream preparation), then link (~0.9 s, of which ~0.61 s is fibers). Follow-ups remain 8b12bc8 (LLVM artifact reuse) and 3b7fa54 (selective loading).","files":null}]}